 ## Background
-The method originates from the application of the WKB (Wentzel-Kramers-Brillouin) approximation to light transport in participating media [S1]. It was introduced in the context of practical rendering of multiple scattering effects, leveraging the concept of the Most Probable Path (MPP) to simplify the high-dimensional path integral [S1]. The approach is part of a broader family of path integral formulations for light transport [G].
